### MaintenanceOrderService - manual test requests (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### Start the service first: npm start   (serves at http://localhost:4004)

@host = http://localhost:4004
@service = {{host}}/odata/v4/maintenance-order

### Sanity check - list a couple of existing orders
GET {{service}}/MaintenanceOrder?$top=3


### 1) Action: createMaintenanceOrder
### Creates a bare MaintenanceOrder header with no operations yet.
POST {{service}}/createMaintenanceOrder
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ID": "MO-TEST1",
  "number": "4500009999",
  "description": "Test order created via createMaintenanceOrder",
  "status": "CRTD",
  "scheduledStartDate": "2026-08-10T08:00:00Z",
  "scheduledEndDate": "2026-08-10T16:00:00Z",
  "assignedWorkCenter": "MECH-01"
}


### 2) Action: addOperation (bound to MaintenanceOrder)
### Adds a single Operation to the order created above.
POST {{service}}/MaintenanceOrder(ID='MO-TEST1')/MaintenanceOrderService.addOperation
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ID": "OP-TEST1",
  "code": "0010",
  "type": "Mechanical",
  "description": "Test operation created via addOperation",
  "status": "CRTD",
  "durationTime": 1.5,
  "durationUnit": "H"
}


### 3) Action: addComponent (bound to Operation)
### Adds a single Component to the operation created above.
POST {{service}}/Operation(ID='OP-TEST1')/MaintenanceOrderService.addComponent
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ID": "COMP-TEST1",
  "quantity": 3,
  "material_ID": "MAT-1000"
}


### Verify the order built up from calls 1-3, with operations and components expanded
GET {{service}}/MaintenanceOrder(ID='MO-TEST1')?$expand=operation($expand=component)


### 4) Action: createMaintenanceOrderDeep
### Creates a MaintenanceOrder together with its operations and their components
### in a single nested call (manual cascade, since operation/component are plain
### Associations rather than Compositions in the domain model).
POST {{service}}/createMaintenanceOrderDeep
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "order": {
    "ID": "MO-DEEP1",
    "number": "4500009998",
    "description": "Deep insert test order",
    "status": "CRTD",
    "scheduledStartDate": "2026-08-11T08:00:00Z",
    "scheduledEndDate": "2026-08-11T16:00:00Z",
    "assignedWorkCenter": "MECH-02",
    "operation": [
      {
        "ID": "OP-DEEP1",
        "code": "0010",
        "type": "Mechanical",
        "description": "Deep-inserted operation 1",
        "status": "CRTD",
        "durationTime": 2,
        "durationUnit": "H",
        "component": [
          { "ID": "COMP-DEEP1", "quantity": 4, "material_ID": "MAT-1000" },
          { "ID": "COMP-DEEP2", "quantity": 1, "material_ID": "MAT-1003" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "ID": "OP-DEEP2",
        "code": "0020",
        "type": "Electrical",
        "description": "Deep-inserted operation 2",
        "status": "CRTD",
        "durationTime": 1,
        "durationUnit": "H",
        "component": []
      }
    ]
  }
}


### Verify the deep-inserted order, with operations and components expanded
GET {{service}}/MaintenanceOrder(ID='MO-DEEP1')?$expand=operation($expand=component)


### 5) Function: mostExpensiveOrder
### Order with the highest total component quantity across all its operations
### (proxy "cost" metric - the model has no price/cost field).
GET {{service}}/mostExpensiveOrder()


### 6) Function: ordersUnfulfillable
### Orders that cannot be fulfilled because at least one required component's
### material has total available stock below the given threshold.
GET {{service}}/ordersUnfulfillable(threshold=50)
